// ============================================================================
//  CCDarkSens — ccdarksens_scan_dmelectron_pattern
//
//  Full DM–electron sensitivity scan over a (mχ, σ_e) grid.
//
//  Pipeline summary
//  ─────────────────
//  1. Load pre-computed dR/dE(mχ, σ_e) rate tables from per-mass CSV files
//     (generated by QEDark / ccdarkphys).
//  2. Fold dR/dE through ChargeIonization → S_true(n_e) expected counts.
//  3. Fold S_true through ε(pattern | n_e) to obtain S_pat per ROI bin.
//  4. Build background B_pat from dark-current + flat d.r.u. migration,
//     or from a pre-computed Bp / Br template.
//  5. For each (mχ, σ_e) grid point compute the profile likelihood ratio:
//       q_μ = 2 · [NLL(S+B, θ̂_μ) − NLL(B, θ̂)]
//     where θ scales the Br background shape nuisance parameter.
//  6. Extract the 90 % CL upper limit by finding where q_μ = Z_α²
//     (default α = 0.90).
//  7. Write the per-mass UL graph and the q(mχ,σ) histogram to a ROOT file.
//
//  Observable spaces   (JSON: experiment.observable_bins)
//  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  • "pattern"  – six SRDM pattern bins {11, 21, 111, 31, 22, 211}
//  • "ne"       – n_e multiplicity bins {1 … 5} with flat ε(n_e)
//
//  Minimiser options   (JSON: run.profile_minimizer)
//  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  • "brent"    – 1-D Brent over θ per σ point (fast default)
//  • "minuit"   – 1-D Minuit over θ; cross-checks Brent result
//  • "minuit2d" – 2-D Minuit over (log₁₀ σ_e, θ) once per mχ
//  • "pydme"    – 2-D Minuit + bisection bracket (closest to pydme output)
//
//  Usage
//  ──────
//    ccdarksens_scan_dmelectron_pattern <config.json>
//  Output: <run.outdir>/scan_dmelectron_pattern.root
//
//  Author: Diego Venegas-Vargas
// ============================================================================

